/**
 * Strided Array Ceil
 *
 * A strided array is a data structure that provides an efficient way to access
 * elements at fixed intervals (strides) from a starting offset. This pattern is
 * commonly used in numerical computing to operate on subsets of arrays or to
 * handle multi-dimensional data in a linearized format.
 *
 * The ceiling function rounds each element of a strided array toward positive
 * infinity, i.e., to the smallest integer greater than or equal to the original
 * value. This operation is useful for discretizing data, preparing integer-based
 * calculations, or implementing certain mathematical algorithms.
 */

